1075:	<h1 class="text-center text-theme-colored2 font-42">About us</h1>
1085:		<div class="col-md-8 about-content">
1088:				King George’s Medical University (KGMU), located in Lucknow, India, is one of South Asia’s leading academic medical institutions, known for its deep commitment to excellence in medical education, groundbreaking research, and world-class clinical care. Established in 1905, KGMU has evolved into a center of academic and clinical distinction with a legacy spanning over a century."
1092:                At the heart of our institution lies one of the largest university-affiliated hospitals in the world, with 4,250 operational beds. This extraordinary capacity enables KGMU to serve as a critical healthcare lifeline not only for the state of Uttar Pradesh but also for the neighboring regions of Bihar, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, and the bordering nation of Nepal. With millions of patient encounters annually, we are one of the busiest and most comprehensive tertiary care providers in the region.
1096:<!-- text about kgmu starts -->
1108:					 Hither-to the College had been affiliated to the Allahabad University. For the first time in 1922 the degrees granted to the successful students was the M.B.B.S. Lucknow instead of the M.B.B.S. Allahabad, as hitherto.
1115:					The College was completed and the work of the first medical session was started in October 1911, though the ceremonial opening of the college building by His Honour Sir John Prescot Hewett did not occur until January 27, 1912.
1147:    Advanced facilities for simulation-based training, biomedical research, public health initiatives, and clinical innovation.
1150:<p><strong>Our institutional mission rests on four pillars:</strong></p>
1168:			KGMU is proud to be a recognized center for excellence by organizations such as the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR) and World Health Organization (WHO). Our collaborations extend across borders, and our graduates contribute meaningfully to healthcare systems around the world.
1169:As we look to the future, KGMU stands at the crossroads of tradition and transformation, committed to advancing health equity, innovation, and medical leadership on both national and global fronts.
1185:<li id="menu-item-30" class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-30"><a href="about_campus.php">About The Campus</a>
1214:                        <td class="text" width="68%" valign="top"> King George's Medical University UP, Lucknow built in 1905, has acquired national & global eminence for contributions in academics, research, and patient care. It caters to need of States of UP and others like Bihar, Chhattisgarh, Madhya Pradesh and neighbouring Nepal and offer medical services to more than 20 crore population. It is the largest Residential Medical University in India with Faculty of Medicine, Faculty of Dental Sciences, Faculty of Nursing and Faculty of Paramedical Sciences. King George Medical University was ranked fifth by the National Institutional Ranking Framework (NIRF) among medical colleges in 2018. </td>
1222:                    <td class="text" height="8" valign="top"> In 2025, King George’s Medical University was awarded the prestigious NAAC A++ Grade by the National Assessment and Accreditation Council, reflecting its commitment to excellence in medical education, research, and healthcare delivery. The Ministry of Education, Government of India, has also shortlisted KGMU among the probable ‘Institutes of Eminence,’ recognising its potential to achieve global standards in medical education and research.</td>
1228:                    <td class="text" height="8" valign="top">The University campus is spread over an area of 7 sq., Km. with more than 50 buildings. There are 2105 hostel rooms, 550 faculty positions, 700 resident doctors and in all 5000 employees. This Prestigious Government University has approximately 5300 undergraduate/Post graduate students, (250 MBBS, 100 BDS seats) getting medical education. This University imparts 181 MD/MS/Diploma Courses in 24 Specialties & 38 DM/M.Ch. courses in 28 super specialties. Postgraduate courses are offered in MD (119 seats in 16 departments), MS (34 seats in 4 departments), Diploma (26 seats in 4 departments), Diploma (PMHS) 35 seats, MDS (27 seats in 7 departments, DM (15 seats in 4 departments), M.Ch. (23 seats in 7 departments), M.Phil (4 seats in Clinical Psychology) and Ph.D (in various departments).</td>
